      "problem": "Given the vectors ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14124424/assets/5ed36f02c74ffab75a56018c8e2fea10e78504738b1dd483f3c1bea4e04052eb.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14124424/assets/e8de856a85bea213513955e6a9652b4f832810394af063acc2366a80565f0e98.svg) find the distance $\\text{d}(\\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y}).$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the distance, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(x,y) & =‖x-y‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{y}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{y}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{y}_{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1-2)^{2}+(2-0)^{2}+(3-(-1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+4+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
